# Data folder

The SCADA records and the incident log belong to the Kocaeli Water and Sewerage
Administration (İSU). They are confidential and are not part of this repository.
Researchers who wish to use them must apply to İSU directly.

To run the code on these or similar data, place the files here:

- One Excel file per district metered area (DMA), named as in `DMA_FILE_MAP` in
  `burst_detection_5models.py` (for example `dya1-04.xlsx`). Expected columns
  (Turkish headers as exported from the utility's SCADA system):
  `Tarih/Saat` (time stamp), `Giriş Basıncı` (inlet pressure), `Debi` (inlet flow),
  `Çıkış Basıncı` (outlet pressure) and, in some DMAs, `Sıvı Tespiti` (liquid detection).
  Native sampling may be 1, 5 or 15 minutes; all series are resampled to 15 minutes.
- `ARIZALAR.xlsx`: the incident log, five columns in this order: city, DMA name
  (as in `DMA_FILE_MAP`), report date and time, description, pipe length (km).

Everything in this folder except this file is ignored by git.
